00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.300
We then have a series
of health checks

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.880
that we could use, which is
really useful, especially

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:51.090
when you're running your
code against a load balancer

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:55.140
or inside of Kubernetes, to be
able to communicate with it,

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:59.370
whether or not your server
can actually handle traffic.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:00.120
So we create this.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.070
We assigned it variable s.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.990
And then for the
