00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:52.490
code and your setup code.

00:24:52.490 --> 00:24:54.170
Because when you
have that seam, all

00:24:54.170 --> 00:24:57.170
of a sudden, this dream of being
able to write your application

00:24:57.170 --> 00:24:59.900
once, deploy it on one cloud,
pick it up and deploy it

00:24:59.900 --> 00:25:03.774
on another cloud becomes
much more feasible.

00:25:03.774 --> 00:25:05.440
Now, again, these are
the supported APIs

00:25:05.440 --> 00:25:06.800
that we're starting with.

00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:08.520
There's still a lot to be done.

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:10.910
This is just a very
small step into getting

00:25:10.910 --> 00:25:13.840
to that world where we can
have this beautiful open-cloud,

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:15.620
multi-cloud story.

00:25:15.620 --> 00:25:18.650
So there's a ton of stuff going
on at the conference right now.

00:25:18.650 --> 00:25:20.330
There's a lot of exciting ideas.

00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:21.980
There's the launch
of native, which

00:25:21.980 --> 00:25:25.212
is really cool, especially
in this open cloud story.

00:25:25.212 --> 00:25:27.420
And a lot of interesting
things to be thinking about.

00:25:27.420 --> 00:25:30.620
So as you walk out of this
room, if you forget everything,

00:25:30.620 --> 00:25:33.260
I want you to at least
remember these three things

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:36.600
about the presentation today.

00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:39.380
So first of all, Go Cloud helps
you develop an application

00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:41.090
that runs on any cloud.

00:25:41.090 --> 00:25:43.070
And that's the big deal here.

00:25:43.070 --> 00:25:44.960
We want Go to be
this great language

00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:49.350
to choose if you want to have
portability across clouds.

00:25:49.350 --> 00:25:51.100
Second of all, we're
starting with support

00:25:51.100 --> 00:25:53.560
from Google Cloud Platform
and Amazon Web Services

00:25:53.560 --> 00:25:56.080
with more to come,
in particular we're

00:25:56.080 --> 00:26:00.240
going to work to have
Azure support on its way.

00:26:00.240 --> 00:26:03.780
And finally, we're looking
for feedback from everyone.

00:26:03.780 --> 00:26:07.020
Understanding more how
each of you are using Go,

00:26:07.020 --> 00:26:09.300
and how you're using
it in the cloud world,

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:11.790
and how you're trying
to achieve multi-cloud

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:13.530
is going to be a big
part of making sure

00:26:13.530 --> 00:26:16.360
that the APIs, as Go
Cloud expands and grows,

00:26:16.360 --> 00:26:18.780
are the ones that are actually
useful to the use cases

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:21.870
that you're all
encountering right now.

00:26:21.870 --> 00:26:25.505
So jump up on
GitHub, check it out.

00:26:25.505 --> 00:26:26.130
Here's the URL.

00:26:26.130 --> 00:26:29.430
It's under the
google.org/go-cloud.

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:31.039
We're just starting
there as we're

00:26:31.039 --> 00:26:32.330
thinking about as it's growing.

00:26:32.330 --> 00:26:34.371
Finally, we've written a
blog post about it today

00:26:34.371 --> 00:26:36.300
that kind of summarizes
some of the ideas

00:26:36.300 --> 00:26:38.466
that we've talked about
today and walks through some

00:26:38.466 --> 00:26:40.050
of more of the examples.

00:26:40.050 --> 00:26:42.120
But I think, really, the
best way to understand

00:26:42.120 --> 00:26:46.380
what this thing is, how powerful
it is is to actually go through

00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:49.392
the tutorial we've got
up on the GitHub repo,

00:26:49.392 --> 00:26:50.850
and try to build
some stuff, or try

00:26:50.850 --> 00:26:52.266
to bring it into
your application,

00:26:52.266 --> 00:26:54.282
and see if it actually works.

00:26:54.282 --> 00:26:56.490
Let us know what works, let
us know what doesn't, let

00:26:56.490 --> 00:26:58.110
us know what's missing.

00:26:58.110 --> 00:26:59.694
We're doing all
development on GitHub,

00:26:59.694 --> 00:27:01.443
so you can send us
issues, you can send us

00:27:01.443 --> 00:27:02.520
PRs straight on GitHub.

00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:04.905
You don't have to worry
about Garrett and so on.

00:27:04.905 --> 00:27:06.390
[LAUGHTER]

00:27:06.390 --> 00:27:06.990
Small thing.

00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:09.160
Anyway, I'm excited.

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.030
I hope you all are too.

00:27:11.030 --> 00:27:12.780
We're just starting
here, and we're really

00:27:12.780 --> 00:27:13.680
hoping you can all join us.

00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:16.260
And we're going to build this
great open cloud story for Go.

00:27:16.260 --> 00:27:17.850
So thank you very much.

00:27:17.850 --> 00:27:21.200
[MUSIC PLAYING]

